# #5839 (#5833's lazy key-moving close in H): the shard root raises the routing generation
# durably, then defers L's close head, and L's arm resolves it.
MODULE: HandOffBoundReceiverArmBelowDeferredReclaimHead
TARGET: HandOffBound
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: L's arm re-claims the deferred generation but keeps the heads earlier closes recorded, below the allocator head, so a foreign record of the window lies above the marker's head (mirrors C's mutation)
PERTURBS: ResolveDeferred
BOUNDS: WithPreArm = TRUE, WithDeferredClose = TRUE, WithTreeWalk = FALSE

--- FIND
    /\ fFence' = Max2(fFence, pendGen)
    /\ hoClosedAt' = Max2(hoClosedAt, next)

--- REPLACE
    /\ fFence' = Max2(fFence, pendGen)
\* MUTATION: the resolution records no head.
    /\ UNCHANGED hoClosedAt

--- END
